OneFit-Engine-C

This repository is an extraction of the C and Fortran engine sources from
OneFit-Engine. Original OneFit code is covered by the Artistic License 2.0;
see LICENSE and the upstream project:
https://github.com/fitteia/OneFit-Engine

Third-party and separately licensed material

1. Florence model (moved out of this repository; NAG code replaced)

local/Florence_c.c/.h and local/Florence_f.f were removed from this
repository and moved to a separate extensions bundle, so this base
repository contains no Florence and no NAG-derived source. The Florence
Fortran once carried NAG Library routines (F01BCF, F02AXF, F02AYF, P01ABF,
P01ABZ); they have been replaced with an independent implementation. The
result is published under the Artistic License 2.0, with the written
permission of the original authors (G. Parigi and A. Kubrak, 2026-10-08),
at https://github.com/fitteia/OneFit-Engine-ext-florence - see its LICENSE
and NOTICE for the required attribution and citations. The original
NAG-derived version is kept in a separate private repository, only for
holders of a NAG Library license.

2. Numerical Recipes routines (replaced)

core/onefit-3.1 and core/onefit-3.1/modelos once used Numerical Recipes
routines (polint, spline/splint, ludcmp/lubksb, gammln/gser/gcf, four1,
qromo/midpnt/gauleg and the nrutil-style allocators). They have been
replaced by independent implementations that keep the historical function
names and one-based calling conventions; this repository contains no
Numerical Recipes code.

3. Minuit

The fitting engine links separately with the Minuit static library. Minuit is
maintained in the sibling repository:
https://github.com/fitteia/OneFit-Engine-minuit
That repository is licensed under the GNU GPL version 2, as stated by the
fork (its sources name no version of their own); see its COPYING file.
Minuit is not relicensed by this repository. Any distribution that links or
bundles Minuit must comply with GPLv2 and provide the corresponding source
and notices.

4. epstopdf

core/onefit-3.1/perl/epstopdf is vendored from CTAN and carries its own
revised 3-clause BSD-style license and copyright notices in the file header.
Those terms remain applicable to that file.

